{"product_id":"the-machine-gunners","title":"The Machine Gunners","description":"\u003cp\u003e`Some bright kid`s got a gun and 2000 rounds of live ammo. And that gun`s no peashooter. It`ll go through a brick wall at a quarter of a mile. ` Chas McGill has the second-best collection of war souvenirs in Garmouth, and he desperately wants it to be the best. When he stumbles across the remains of a German bomber crashed in the woods - its shiny, black machine-gun still intact - he grabs his chance. Soon he`s masterminding his own war effort with dangerous and unexpected results...‰غ‌...not just the best book so far written for children about the Second World War, but also a metaphor for now. ‰غد - Aidan Chambers, ‰غد Times Literary Supplement‰غ‌ .\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 129 x 197\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Robert Westall\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9780330397858\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Paperback\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 224\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookhero.ae","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45297448648857,"sku":"4RF9780330397858","price":10.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/TheMachineGunnersRobertWestall.jpg?v=1752084511","url":"https:\/\/bookhero.ae\/products\/the-machine-gunners","provider":"Dubai - Buy Used\/Second-Hand Books - BookHero","version":"1.0","type":"link"}